From 46ca14950dc76004c5df355ce2c975a77c50041a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Patch Verification <patch-verification@localhost>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 16:29:40 +0800
Subject: perf(query-corruption): [QCT-007] simplify query opt-in and warning
 cleanup

Problem
The original opt-in walks scan sources, Pipeline compatibility and remote runtime filters even though diagnostic delivery is now explicitly best-effort. Warning cleanup also inspects statement types when no previous diagnostic exists.

Implementation
Replace plan walks with fixed-size eligibility checks. Allow EXPLAIN ANALYZE, mixed sources and remote runtime filters; reuse the existing OUTFILE boolean and retain DefaultCoordinator type safety. Short-circuit on the global switch and refresh opt-in state for every existing execution attempt. Return early from beginStatement when no warning is stored. Update requirements, design, deployment guidance and QCT-007 evidence.

Compatibility
Keep internal/write/OUTFILE/short-circuit/Arrow/HTTP-raw exclusions and all BE error boundaries unchanged. Do not change SHOW WARNINGS/ERRORS, planning, scheduling, cancellation, Query Cache, or wire definitions. Mixed queries tolerate only already-integrated local readers; pure external HTTP queries may gain false/empty diagnostic fields. A missing warning no longer certifies that no tolerated corruption occurred.

Tests
Passed FE Maven package and 41 tests across 9 classes twice, with zero failures, errors or skips, in the isolated QCT arm64 container. Includes real optimized-plan checks, no-plan-walk guards, warning lifecycle, MySQL packets, both JDBC drivers and HTTP socket regressions using simulated BE statistics. The first package had UNKNOWN version metadata; the repeat package uses an explicit QCT-007 worktree marker, not a release commit label. Verified source checksums and git diff --check.
Not run: performance acceptance or profiling, explicitly deferred by the user; new physical-corruption integration coverage, full BE tests/sanitizers, or BE rebuild because BE code is unchanged. Historical QCT-006 performance is not evidence for this commit. No push or patch-bundle regeneration.
